---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
// Plain-language privacy notice. Keep it in step with what the site actually uses:
// Mailchimp (Garden signups), Netlify (hosting, Let's Talk form), Spotify and
// YouTube embeds, Calendly links, and Google Analytics once it's added.
const updated = 'November 3, 2026';
---
<Base title="Privacy | The Soul Mami" description="How The Soul Mami website handles your information: what's collected, why, who helps, and how to get it changed or removed.">

  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
      <h1>Your info, <em class="soul">handled with care</em></h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The short version: I only collect what I need to write to you and
        reply to you, I never sell it, and you can ask me to change or
        delete it any time.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section policy" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="wrap prose">

      <h2>Who I am</h2>
      <p>
        This website is run by Eliana, the Soul Mami ("I", "me"). When this
        page talks about "your information," it means anything that
        identifies you, like your name or email address.
      </p>

      <h2>What I collect and why</h2>
      <h3>When you join my Garden</h3>
      <p>
        You give me your email address and, if you like, your first name.
        I use them to send you my letters: journal entries, new songs,
        tools, and news about the Journaling Hive. Signups are stored with
        Mailchimp, my email service. Every letter has an unsubscribe link,
        and one click takes you off the list.
      </p>
      <h3>When you write to me through Let's Talk</h3>
      <p>
        You give me your name, your email address, and your message. I use
        them only to reply to you. The form is handled by Netlify, the
        company that hosts this website.
      </p>
      <h3>When you write back on a journal entry</h3>
      <p>
        If you write back on a journal entry, your name and words appear
        publicly on that page. Comments are collected through Netlify. If
        you'd like one removed, <a href="/lets-talk/">send me a note</a>.
      </p>
      <h3>When you book a session</h3>
      <p>
        Booking links open Calendly, which collects the details it needs
        to schedule your time with me. Calendly's own privacy policy
        applies there.
      </p>
      <h3>When you simply visit</h3>
      <p>
        Like most websites, the servers that host this site keep basic
        technical logs (such as your browser type and IP address) to keep
        it running and secure. I may also use Google Analytics to see, in
        general terms, how many people visit and which pages they read.
        That helps me make the site better. It uses cookies, and it
        doesn't tell me who you are.
      </p>

      <h2>Music and video players</h2>
      <p>
        Some pages include players from Spotify and YouTube. When you press
        play, or sometimes just when the page loads, those services may set
        their own cookies and collect information under their own privacy
        policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Who I share it with</h2>
      <p>
        Nobody gets your information to market to you. I never sell it or
        trade it. It's only shared with the services that help me run this
        site and my letters: Mailchimp (email), Netlify (hosting and the
        contact form), Calendly (bookings), and Google (analytics). Each of
        them protects it under their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
      <p>
        You stay on my list until you unsubscribe or ask me to remove you.
        Messages you send me are kept as long as I need them to reply and
        follow up, and deleted when they're no longer needed.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul class="policy-list">
        <li>Unsubscribe from my letters any time, using the link at the bottom of every email.</li>
        <li>Ask to see the information I have about you, or ask me to correct or delete it.</li>
        <li>Block or clear cookies in your browser settings. The site still works without them.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To ask for any of these, just <a href="/lets-talk/">send me a note</a>
        and tell me what you need. I'll take care of it.
      </p>

      <h2>Kids</h2>
      <p>
        This site is meant for adults. I don't knowingly collect
        information from anyone under 16.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If anything here changes, I'll update this page and the date at
        the top.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem) 2rem; }
  .policy h2 { margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 1.9rem); }
  .policy h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .policy h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .policy-list { padding-left: 1.2rem; display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .policy-list li::marker { color: var(--honey); }
</style>
